; The canonical change from S1 to S2.
;
; S1 |- S2. S1 gave a declaration a type. S2 lets a type mention a value.
;
; A family is declared with a telescope, each constructor says which index it
; lands on, and a function type may bind its argument so the result can refer
; to it. Types are compared after computation rather than before, so a type
; that adds up is accepted and one that does not is a type error.
;
; Equality is not a primitive. It is a family whose only constructor lands on
; the index where both sides agree, so a proof is an ordinary value.
(change
  (kind foundation)
  (name "S1->S2")
  (predecessor (foundation-of "foundations/S1"))
  (delta-meta (file "changes/S1-S2/delta-meta.canon"))
  (delta-grammar (file "changes/S1-S2/delta-grammar.canon"))
  (feature
    (feature
      (name "the dependent core")
      (programs [
        (file "features/strata/depend.generated.meta")
      ])
      (sources [
        (text-file "features/strata/depend.meta")
        (text-file "languages/strata/strata.grammar")
        (text-file "languages/strata/strata.meta")
      ]))))
